From 3aecef67562161ef894ed600c61d509a594d5bcf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Silas=20M=C3=BCller?= <dev@silasmueller.de>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 09:54:29 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] vfio-user: support VFIO_USER_DEVICE_GET_REGION_IO_FDS

The vfio-user specification defines VFIO_USER_DEVICE_GET_REGION_IO_FDS
(command 6): the client asks for the sub-regions of a region that the
server wants accessed through file descriptors, and configures them, for
example as KVM ioeventfds, so that guest writes there reach the server
without a round trip through the client. The server answered it with
UnsupportedCommand.

Client: get_region_io_fds(index) sends argsz, flags 0, index and count 0
and receives the reply with its SCM_RIGHTS descriptors.
parse_region_io_fds_reply() accepts the reply only in the form the
specification lays out ("VFIO_USER_DEVICE_GET_REGION_IO_FDS", "Reply",
and "Sub-Region IO FD info format (ioeventfd)" and "(ioregionfd)"):
argsz, flags 0, the requested index and count at offsets 0 to 12, argsz
equal to 16 + count * 40 and to the payload size, and 40-byte entries at
16 + i * 40 with offset, size, fd_index, type and flags at 0, 8, 16, 20
and 24 and datamatch (ioeventfd, type 0) or user_data (ioregionfd,
type 1) at 32. Anything else is Error::InvalidReply, after which the
stream is still in step. A reply whose argsz exceeds the request's
("Message sizes") is asked for again with that argsz. A refused request
returns Error::ErrorReply and leaves the stream in step: servers up to
0.1.6 answer the request before reading its payload, then parse the
payload as a header of command 0 and answer that too, so the client
follows an error reply with a DEVICE_GET_INFO round trip and drops one
stray header-only error reply ahead of it.

Server: add_ioeventfd(index, IoEventFdSubRegion) declares an ioeventfd
sub-region (offset, size, KVM_IOEVENTFD flags, datamatch, eventfd) within
a region. The request is answered with 40-byte ioeventfd entries; a reply
that does not fit argsz carries only the fixed part with the argsz needed.
Sub-regions sharing one eventfd send it once, and no reply carries more
descriptors than the max_msg_fds the client announced in VFIO_USER_VERSION
(1 when absent).

Not wire-compatible with libvfio-user on this message: libvfio-user
(include/vfio-user.h:178-187) sends 48-byte ioeventfd entries with
shadow_mem_fd_index at 28, shadow_offset at 32 and datamatch at 40, for
its out-of-tree shadow ioeventfd (type 2), where the specification has
padding at 28 and datamatch at 32. Such a reply is refused rather than
read with the wrong datamatch. The type values 0 and 1 are libvfio-user's;
the specification names the types without numbers. The specification's
entry offset formula, i * ((argsz - 32) / count), contradicts its reply
table (the array starts at 16); with the exact size check the entries are
at 16 + i * 40.

Tests: the reply parser against hand-built buffers in the specification's
byte layout (entries of both types, truncation, malformed replies) and
against a libvfio-user-shaped reply, the server's reply bytes, a
client/server round trip with descriptor sharing, truncation and
max_msg_fds, and a server that does not implement the request.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
